(ANSA) - ROME, 04 NOV - Bob Dylan met Pope Leo XIV at the Vatican Wednesday.
&#034;Today, I accompanied Bob Dylan to meet Pope Leo, together with Andrea Monda (editor of Vatican daily L&#039;Osservatore Romano),&#034; wrote Father Antonio Spadaro, editor in chief of the Jesuit-affiliated journal La Civiltà Cattolica, on social media, where he also shared two photos of Dylan (wearing a black hood) and Leo.
&#034;It was an incredibly moving experience—a meeting that felt truly historic—with the constant sense that, with every step taken through the Apostolic Palace, anything could happen!&#034;
